  "result": "Perfect! Customer merge is complete. All 324 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **SAME_CUSTOMER error** added to src/errors.js for duplicate merge attempts\n\n2. **mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)** function in src/customers.js that:\n   - Removes the fromId customer from the customers array\n   - Reassigns all invoices from fromId to intoId\n   - Normalizes both IDs (trim whitespace, uppercase)\n   - Never mutates input arrays (returns new copies)\n   - Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` with merged data\n   \n   Validation:\n   - Returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if either ID doesn't exist\n   - Returns SAME_CUSTOMER if both IDs normalize to the same customer\n\n3. **14 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Basic merge (removes one customer, updates invoices)\n   - Error handling (missing customers, duplicate merge)\n   - ID normalization (case-insensitive, spaces trimmed)\n   - Non-mutation guarantee\n   - Multiple invoices from the same customer\n   - Edge cases (no invoices, multiple other customers)\n   - Data preservation (invoice fields remain intact)\n   - Object copying (changes don't affect originals)\n\nEnables deduplication when discovering that two customer records are actually the same entity, consolidating all billing history under one record.",
